++ * outright. A kprobe reaches the same call site from the other side: kprobe
++ * instruction pages are whitelisted with the hypervisor, so a breakpoint is
++ * accepted where a plain write is not. Every slot therefore tries the write
++ * first and diverts the handler it points at when the write is refused.
